IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `fbtaa-employee`

-- Fringe Benefits Tax Assessment Act 1986 (Cth) -- THE EMPLOYER'S SEAT LAYER.
--
-- SEAT: the employer -- a small business owner or a company that provides benefits to employees, and on whom the tax falls
-- (s 66(1): the tax "is payable by the employer"). "What is my fringe benefits taxable amount, how much FBT do I pay, and by
-- when? What is the taxable value of the car or loan I provide? Must I report an employee's fringe benefits, and how much?"
--
-- This is the SECOND seat on this encoding, beside the employee's (fbtaa-employee.l4), under the ruling of 21 October 2026
-- on more than one seat. Where a question is the employee's question asked from the other side, it calls the rule in
-- fbtaa-employee.l4 and restates none, so the two seats cannot disagree; the mirror cases in fbtaa-cases-employer.l4 show it.
-- The fringe benefits taxable amount and the return and payment dates are this layer's own rules (the employee meets
-- neither).
--
-- PLAIN INPUTS, each with an @desc worded from the employer's seat. NAMES: every name defined here begins "As the employer, ".
--
-- Formulas: ss 5B(1B), 5B(1C) from ../../registers/source-bundle/C2004A03280.formulas.md. Rate: Fringe Benefits Tax Act 1986
-- ss 6, 6A, through `the rate of fringe benefits tax for` in fbtaa-employee.l4. The GST rate is an input (the GST Act's).
--
-- NOT ENCODED here: working out the type 1 and type 2 aggregate fringe benefits amounts benefit by benefit (s 5C; which
-- benefits are GST-creditable, s 149A, is the employer's input), the s 5B(1D)-(1M) addition for s 57A employers, s 135G,
-- instalments (Part VII), the rebate (s 65J), and everything listed as out in fbtaa-employee.l4.

§ `Fringe Benefits Tax Assessment Act 1986 -- the employer's questions`

§§ `s 5B, s 66, Fringe Benefits Tax Act s 6 -- my fringe benefits taxable amount and the tax`

-- s 5B(1A): the taxable amount "is the sum of the subsection (1B) amount and the subsection (1C) amount". (1B): Type 1
-- aggregate fringe benefits amount x (FBT rate + GST rate) / ((1 - FBT rate) x (1 + GST rate) x FBT rate). (1C): Type 2
-- aggregate fringe benefits amount x 1 / (1 - FBT rate). s 5C(3): the type 1 amount is the taxable values of the fringe
-- benefits that are GST-creditable benefits (s 149A: the provider was entitled to an input tax credit); (4): type 2 is the
-- rest.
GIVEN `type 1 amount` IS A NUMBER
      `type 2 amount` IS A NUMBER
      `FBT rate` IS A NUMBER
      `GST rate` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`As the employer, the taxable amount at rates` MEANS
    (`type 1 amount` TIMES ((`FBT rate` PLUS `GST rate`) DIVIDED BY ((1 MINUS `FBT rate`) TIMES (1 PLUS `GST rate`) TIMES `FBT rate`)))
    PLUS (`type 2 amount` TIMES (1 DIVIDED BY (1 MINUS `FBT rate`)))

@export As the employer, what is my fringe benefits taxable amount for the FBT year (s 5B)?
GIVEN `the FBT year starting in` IS A NUMBER @desc The calendar year in which the FBT year starts (1 April to 31 March)
      `my type 1 aggregate fringe benefits amount` IS A NUMBER @desc The total taxable value of the fringe benefits you provided in the year for which you (or the provider) could claim a GST input tax credit (GST-creditable benefits)
      `my type 2 aggregate fringe benefits amount` IS A NUMBER @desc The total taxable value of your other fringe benefits for the year
      `the GST rate` IS A NUMBER @desc The rate of GST for the year, as a fraction (0.1 for 10%)
GIVETH AN `Answer` NUMBER
`As the employer, my fringe benefits taxable amount` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the rate of fringe benefits tax for` `the FBT year starting in`
    WHEN `not covered` r THEN `not covered` r
    WHEN `answered` rate THEN `answered` (`As the employer, the taxable amount at rates` `my type 1 aggregate fringe benefits amount` `my type 2 aggregate fringe benefits amount` rate `the GST rate`)

-- s 66(1): tax "is payable by the employer". Fringe Benefits Tax Act 1986 s 5: tax "is imposed in respect of the fringe
-- benefits taxable amount"; s 6: at 47% (49% for the years of tax starting 1 April 2015 and 2016, s 6A).
@export As the employer, how much fringe benefits tax must I pay for the FBT year?
GIVEN `the FBT year starting in` IS A NUMBER @desc The calendar year in which the FBT year starts (1 April to 31 March)
      `my type 1 aggregate fringe benefits amount` IS A NUMBER @desc The total taxable value of your GST-creditable fringe benefits for the year
      `my type 2 aggregate fringe benefits amount` IS A NUMBER @desc The total taxable value of your other fringe benefits for the year
      `the GST rate` IS A NUMBER @desc The rate of GST for the year, as a fraction (0.1 for 10%)
GIVETH AN `Answer` NUMBER
`As the employer, the fringe benefits tax I must pay` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the rate of fringe benefits tax for` `the FBT year starting in`
    WHEN `not covered` r THEN `not covered` r
    WHEN `answered` rate THEN `answered` (rate TIMES (`As the employer, the taxable amount at rates` `my type 1 aggregate fringe benefits amount` `my type 2 aggregate fringe benefits amount` rate `the GST rate`))

§§ `ss 68, 90 -- when my return and the tax are due`

-- s 68: where there is a fringe benefits taxable amount, the employer "shall ... furnish to the Commissioner a return not later
-- than 21 May in the next year of tax or such later date as the Commissioner allows". s 90: the tax "becomes due and payable ...
-- on 21 May in the next year of tax". The Commissioner's later date is not encoded.
@export As the employer, by when must I lodge my FBT return and pay the tax?
GIVEN `the FBT year starting in` IS A NUMBER @desc The calendar year in which the FBT year starts (1 April to 31 March)
GIVETH A DATE
`As the employer, the day my FBT return and tax are due` MEANS Date 21 5 (`the FBT year starting in` PLUS 1)

§§ `Mirror questions -- the employee's rules, from the employer's side`

@export As the employer, what is the taxable value of the car I provide to this employee, under the statutory formula (s 9)?
GIVEN `the car's cost price` IS A NUMBER @desc The cost price of the car to you (or your associate) when you first held it, or its leased car value then if leased (GST-inclusive, without registration or stamp duty)
      `the day I first held the car` IS A DATE @desc The earliest day you (or your associate) held the car
      `the FBT year starting in` IS A NUMBER @desc The calendar year in which the FBT year starts (1 April to 31 March)
      `the cost of non-business accessories added` IS A NUMBER @desc The cost price of non-business accessories fitted after you first held the car and still fitted during the year; 0 if none
      `the days the car was available to the employee` IS A NUMBER @desc The number of days in the FBT year on which the car was provided to the employee (available for private use)
      `what the employee paid towards the car` IS A NUMBER @desc What the employee paid towards the car during the year and you did not reimburse (fuel only if you received the declaration or receipts in time)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`As the employer, the taxable value of the car` MEANS
    `The taxable value of my car` `the car's cost price` `the day I first held the car` `the FBT year starting in` `the cost of non-business accessories added` `the days the car was available to the employee` `what the employee paid towards the car`

@export As the employer, what is the taxable value of the loan I made to this employee (s 18)?
GIVEN `the loan balance` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount the employee owed you on the loan each day (taken as the same through the period)
      `the days it was owed in the year` IS A NUMBER @desc The number of days in the FBT year on which the employee was obliged to repay the loan
      `the benchmark interest rate` IS A NUMBER @desc The statutory interest rate for the FBT year, as a percentage (the Reserve Bank's large bank housing lenders variable rate for owner-occupied housing last published before 1 April)
      `the interest that accrued on the loan` IS A NUMBER @desc The interest that actually accrued on the loan for the year
GIVETH A NUMBER
`As the employer, the taxable value of the loan` MEANS
    `The taxable value of my loan` `the loan balance` `the days it was owed in the year` `the benchmark interest rate` `the interest that accrued on the loan`

@export As the employer, is the electric car I provide to this employee exempt (s 8A)?
GIVEN `the employee is a current employee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person is your current employee
      `the kind of car` IS A `The kind of car` @desc What kind of car it is, when the benefit is provided
      `luxury car tax was payable on it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether luxury car tax became payable on a supply or importation of the car before the benefit was provided
GIVETH A `Is my car exempt`
`As the employer, is the electric car exempt` MEANS
    `Is my electric car exempt` `the employee is a current employee` `the kind of car` `luxury car tax was payable on it`

@export As the employer, what reportable fringe benefits amount must I report for this employee (s 135P)?
GIVEN `the employee's individual fringe benefits amount` IS A NUMBER @desc The total taxable value of the fringe benefits you provided to this employee in the FBT year, including an exempt electric car, but leaving out car parking, meal entertainment that is not salary packaged, and the other excluded fringe benefits
      `the FBT year starting in` IS A NUMBER @desc The calendar year in which the FBT year started
      `I am a charity, hospital, ambulance service or other s 57A or s 58 employer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a public benevolent institution, health promotion charity, public or non-profit hospital, public ambulance service, or an employer of the kind in s 58
GIVETH AN `Answer` NUMBER
`As the employer, the reportable fringe benefits amount` MEANS
    `My reportable fringe benefits amount` `the employee's individual fringe benefits amount` `the FBT year starting in` `I am a charity, hospital, ambulance service or other s 57A or s 58 employer`
